Bug 2068614 - Set mSourceNode after hiding the previous tooltip in MouseMove.  a=dmeehan DONTBUILD

Follow-up to https://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/rev/3bfa78cb60f7

comm/mail/components/im/test/browser/browser_tooltips.js regressed on
bug 2001695 and passes again with this: its second task moves the mouse into a
fresh conversation browser while a node from the first task is still tracked.

nsXULTooltipListener::MouseMove() recorded mSourceNode and ran
CheckTreeBodyMove() before hiding the tooltip of the node the mouse just left.
Both of those HideTooltip() paths end in DestroyTooltip(), which clears
mSourceNode, so the timer armed a few lines later fired into a ShowTooltip()
with no source node: GetTooltipFor(nullptr) fails and no tooltip is shown for
the new node, ever.

Move the mSourceNode assignment and CheckTreeBodyMove() call to after the teardown,
so the source survives for the timer callback.

Original Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322942

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336493


